  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Quiquesetinerviuside B may interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through a series of target relationships. This compound is predicted to act as a target of SN12K1 and Rha(a1-3)[coumaroyl(3-OH)(-4)]Glc(b)-O-EtPh, both of which are implicated in targeting the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. Additionally, Quiquesetinerviuside B is predicted to target Neuropilin-2, which in turn targets a compound that also interacts with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. These findings collectively indicate a potential pathway through which Quiquesetinerviuside B may influence the activity of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be elucidated. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, suggesting a plausible biological relationship, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction and functional role of Quiquesetinerviuside B in this context.",
